# Cloudflare Pages header overrides.
#
# Cloudflare merges every rule that matches a request, so `/*` carries the
# security headers for the whole site and `/_astro/*` adds long caching on top
# for hashed build assets — both apply to those requests without conflict.

# Security headers, site-wide.
#
# HSTS stops the first request from ever going out over plain HTTP for a year;
# `includeSubDomains` extends that to any subdomain. `preload` is deliberately
# left off — preloading is effectively irreversible, so it should be an
# informed choice, not a default.
#
# CSP is enforcing. It was proven Report-Only first — browser-tested against
# the built site with zero violations, which is how the inline Astro island
# runtime hashes (scripts/csp-hashes.mjs) and the Vue/Zod eval fixes landed.
# Reports still post to /api/csp-report (see functions/api/csp-report.ts), so
# a violation that only shows up in production stays visible in the Pages
# Function logs — flip the header name back to Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only
# to return to watching without blocking.
#
# Why each exception exists:
#   script-src  + challenges.cloudflare.com  — the Turnstile widget script
#   script-src  + 'sha256-…'                — Astro's inline island runtime (stamped at build)
#   frame-src   + challenges.cloudflare.com  — the Turnstile iframe it mounts
#   connect-src + sgp.cloud.appwrite.io      — the Appwrite API the client calls
#   connect-src + challenges.cloudflare.com  — widget chatter from the top frame
#   style-src   'unsafe-inline'              — inline <style> and style= attributes
#   img/font-src data: blob:                 — inline SVGs and object URLs
#   object-src 'none', frame-ancestors 'none' — hard stops, no legitimate use
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com __CSP_SCRIPT_HASHES__; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io wss://sgp.cloud.appwrite.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; report-uri /api/csp-report

# Hashed build assets cannot change without a new file name, so the etag dance
# Cloudflare serves by default (`max-age=0, must-revalidate`) is pure round
# trips on every revisit. HTML keeps the default: it must stay revalidated so a
# deploy goes live immediately.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
